    {"id": "fork_1", "url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/src/models/deepseek4.cpp#L289", "revision": "3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5", "evidence": "CODE_PRESENT", "finding": "Host Engram actual implementation, not flag: create_tensor TENSOR_HOST; CPU hash/raw FP8 dequant rows, transferred graph lookup buffer. No forced disk streaming. mmap normal OS backing vs --no-mmap RAM allocation. 881.78GiB RAM can contain entire ~467.35GiB GGUF with headroom, excluding allocations/caches/context/OS. NVMe path optional, originally compensates 125.7GiB author RAM.", "corroborating_url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/src/llama-graph.cpp#L178"},
    {"id": "fork_2", "url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c#L286", "revision": "3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5", "evidence": "CODE_PRESENT", "finding": "CPU MoE follows real graph and kernels: model ffn_exps -> generic build_moe_ffn -> ggml_mul_mat_id; CPU type trait maps MXFP4 to vec_dot_mxfp4_q8_0 and generic MUL_MAT_ID uses trait; x86 AVX2 implementation. CPU override supported. This proves code path present, not full model validated.", "corroborating_url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c#L918"},
    {"id": "fork_3", "url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/src/llama-model.cpp#L1400", "revision": "3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5", "evidence": "CODE_PRESENT", "finding": "Two GPU layer split loader present: devices -> normalized split -> layer assigned buffer; dense layers can span CUDA0/CUDA1 while CPU override routes experts and host flags pin Engram. Tensor split mode explicitly unsupported for DEEPSEEK41; use layer mode. No full two-GPU hybrid author validation found.", "corroborating_url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/src/llama-arch.cpp#L1036"},
    {"id": "fork_4", "url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/CMakeLists.txt#L40", "revision": "3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5", "evidence": "CODE_PRESENT", "finding": "SM120 explicit CMake 120a-real requires CUDA>=12.8; native MXFP4 GPU MMQ availability tests compiled Blackwell code>=1200. This is closer RTX5090 evidence but not dual RTX PRO6000/Linux validation.", "corroborating_url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh#L360"},
    {"id": "fork_5", "url": "https://github.com/JigSawPT/llama.cpp/blob/3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5/convert_hf_to_gguf.py#L120", "revision": "3b6fcfe4f7e2c282076f0c159278d3acfa3ad4e5", "evidence": "CODE_PRESENT", "finding": "Conversion --engram is mandatory for original-model semantics; default omits tables and output differs. Requires matching custom layout; upstream conversion PR layout incompatible with author GGUF. Standard author command --outtype bf16 --engram then split. Source+one converted output1.012TB; retaining monolithic+split output1.514TB before scratch/draft/vision. Converted author GGUF download avoids source+conversion duplication if separately approved.", "corroborating_url": "https://huggingface.co/JigSawPT/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-GGUF/blob/764e7eb0fc6272d664df015ac87964a52d151803/README.md"},
